# .cmd/.bat files are GBK (cp936) encoded with CRLF line endings and contain
# non-ASCII text. Git's automatic newline normalization (core.autocrlf / eol)
# would convert CRLF to LF, and a UTF-8 re-encode would break them under code
# page 936 (symptoms: bogus errors like "'obreak' is not recognized").
# Mark them binary so git never touches them.
*.cmd binary
*.bat binary

# Everything else is UTF-8 with LF for cross-platform consistency
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.ps1  binary
